== How to enter flash mode ==
=== Fastboot mode ===
Power on with the volume keys held: the stock bootloader's own fastboot, which is also what
restores Android from a backup boot image. (Confirm the exact combination on the device page once
verified.)

=== Unisoc flashing mode ===
Power on with volume up held and connect with a flashing tool. `spd_dump` is the way back if the
phone reaches neither fastboot nor U-Boot.

== Installation ==
The port is not in pmaports yet; build it from the [https://github.com/Seuj09/pmos-infinix-x6525
port repository] and follow that repository's FIRST_BOOT.md. In short: install to a microSD card
with <code>pmbootstrap install --sdcard=/dev/sdX</code>, flash U-Boot into <code>boot_a</code> with
<code>pmbootstrap flasher flash_kernel</code>, insert the card and boot from it.

<code>pmbootstrap flasher flash_rootfs</code> must not be used: it would write the whole disk image
into the <code>super</code> partition, where U-Boot cannot see the partition table nested inside it.
Only <code>boot_a</code> is written on the eMMC, so Android and its data stay where they are, and
<code>fastboot flash boot_a &lt;backup boot.img&gt;</code> is the way back.

